Copyright (c) 2026 Proximi.io. All rights reserved.


1. WHAT THIS DOCUMENT COVERS

1.1  "SDK" means the precompiled Proximi.io iOS SDK distributed from the
     repository github.com/proximiio/proximiio-sdk-ios-binary: the
     `ProximiioBinary.xcframework` attached to each release, the package
     manifest, the podspec, the one-line source shims, and the accompanying
     documentation. It does not mean the SDK's source code, which is not
     published.

1.2  "You" means the legal entity exercising the rights below, and every entity
     that entity controls.

1.3  The SDK is licensed, not sold. Proximi.io grants you the rights in
     clause 2 and keeps everything else.


2. LICENCE GRANT

Subject to clauses 3, 7 and 11, Proximi.io grants you a non-exclusive,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable, worldwide licence, for the term described
in clause 11, to:

2.1  download, install and store copies of the SDK;

2.2  integrate the SDK into applications you develop ("your Applications") and
     make copies of it as your build process requires;

2.3  distribute the SDK, in its compiled form, embedded inside your Applications
     — through the Apple App Store, TestFlight, Apple Business Manager, an
     enterprise distribution programme, or any equivalent channel — to end users
     of those Applications; and

2.4  use the SDK internally for development, testing and support of your
     Applications.

2.5  No licence to end users. Your end users receive the SDK only as an
     inseparable part of your Application. They get no rights in the SDK of
     their own, and your Application's own end-user terms must not purport to
     grant them any.


3. WHAT THE LICENCE DOES NOT ALLOW

Except where a mandatory law gives you a right that cannot be contracted away
(and then only to the extent of that right), you must not, and must not permit
anyone else to:

3.1  reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or otherwise attempt to derive
     the source code, algorithms, model parameters or internal design of the
     SDK, whether by static analysis of the binary, instrumentation of it at
     runtime, or any other means;

3.2  extract, isolate, re-link or repackage any part of the SDK so that it can
     be used outside one of your Applications — including lifting the
     xcframework, or any object code, symbol or resource out of it, into
     another library, framework, package, container or service;

3.3  distribute, publish, sublicense, sell, rent, lease, lend or otherwise make
     the SDK available as a library, SDK, package, component or hosted service,
     whether on its own or bundled with other software. Clause 2.3 is the only
     redistribution this licence permits: inside your Application, as part of
     its compiled product;

3.4  use the SDK, or anything you learn from it, to build, train, improve or
     operate a product that competes with the SDK or with the Proximi.io
     platform — including an indoor positioning, indoor wayfinding, or venue
     mapping SDK or service;

3.5  remove, obscure or alter any copyright notice, licence text, attribution,
     product identifier or code signature in the SDK or in the third-party
     components it brings with it;

3.6  circumvent or disable any licence check, token validation, quota or usage
     measurement in the SDK or in the Proximi.io services it talks to, or use
     the SDK with credentials you are not entitled to use; or

3.7  represent the SDK, or the positioning it produces, as your own technology
     in a way that misstates its origin.


4. THE PUBLIC REPOSITORY IS NOT A PUBLIC LICENCE

4.1  The distribution repository is public so that Swift Package Manager and
     CocoaPods can resolve it without credentials. That is a mechanical
     necessity of how those tools fetch packages, not an offer of open-source
     terms.

4.2  Being able to read the repository, clone it, or download a release asset
     gives you no licence to use the SDK. The rights in clause 2 exist only
     while you hold a valid Proximi.io commercial agreement (clause 7). Absent
     that agreement, any use beyond evaluating whether to enter into one is
     unlicensed.

4.3  The SDK is not open source, and nothing about the repository's visibility
     makes it so. No open-source licence — permissive or copyleft — applies to
     the Proximi.io portions of this distribution. The third-party components
     in clause 8 carry their own licences, and those apply only to those
     components.


5. OWNERSHIP

5.1  Proximi.io and its licensors own the SDK and every intellectual property
     right in it, including the positioning, dead-reckoning, geofencing and
     wayfinding methods it implements. Nothing in this licence transfers any
     of that to you.

5.2  You own your Applications and everything you write. Integrating the SDK
     gives Proximi.io no rights in your code.

5.3  This licence grants no trademark rights. You may state factually that your
     Application uses Proximi.io technology; any other use of Proximi.io's
     names or logos needs written permission.

5.4  If you send Proximi.io feedback, bug reports or suggestions, Proximi.io may
     use them without obligation to you. This does not give Proximi.io any
     licence to your Applications or to your data.


6. THE SDK NEEDS A PROXIMI.IO ACCOUNT

6.1  The SDK does nothing useful on its own. It requires a Proximi.io account
     and a valid token, and it works against Proximi.io services whose terms,
     availability and pricing are set in your commercial agreement, not here.

6.2  This licence does not entitle you to those services, to any service level,
     to support, or to any future release of the SDK. Those come from the
     commercial agreement, if it provides them.


7. RELATIONSHIP TO YOUR COMMERCIAL AGREEMENT

7.1  This file states the terms on which the binary SDK may be used. Your
     separate written commercial agreement with Proximi.io — subscription
     agreement, master services agreement, order form, or equivalent — states
     the commercial relationship: fees, term, service levels, data processing,
     support, and the like.

7.2  Where the two conflict, the commercial agreement prevails, and this file
     is read as narrowed or widened to match it. If your commercial agreement
     grants you rights this file does not, you have those rights. If it imposes
     restrictions this file does not, those restrictions apply.

7.3  If you have no commercial agreement with Proximi.io, this file governs on
     its own, and clause 4.2 applies: you have no licence to use the SDK in
     production.

7.4  This file is not an entire-agreement clause and does not replace anything
     you have already signed.


8. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The SDK brings third-party software with it. Those components are licensed to
you by their own licensors under their own terms, not by Proximi.io under this
licence, and clause 3 does not restrict what those licences permit. Clause 9's
disclaimer and clause 10's liability limits apply to them as they reach you
through the SDK.

8.1  GRDB.swift — MIT licence.

     GRDB.swift (github.com/groue/GRDB.swift) is compiled into
     `ProximiioBinary.xcframework`, and is also declared as a package
     dependency so that it resolves in your own build. Either way, your
     Application ships GRDB code.

     The MIT licence requires that the notice below travel with every copy.
     Reproduce it in your Application's acknowledgements or legal screen:

     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Copyright (C) 2015-2025 Gwendal Roué

     Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a
     copy of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"),
     to deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation
     the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense,
     and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the
     Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

     The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in
     all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

     THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
     IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
     FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL
     THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
     LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING
     FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER
     DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

8.2  SQLite — no obligation on you.

     The SDK links SQLite through Apple's system library,
     `/usr/lib/libsqlite3.dylib`. Proximi.io does not distribute SQLite to you;
     Apple does, as part of iOS. Your use of it is covered by your Apple
     developer agreements. SQLite itself is in the public domain and asks for
     no attribution.

8.3  Nothing else ships.

     The SDK binary declares no dynamic dependency other than the Apple system
     frameworks and `libsqlite3.dylib`, and embeds no third-party code besides
     GRDB. In particular it embeds no third-party RTLS vendor SDK: the Quuppa
     and Blueiot integrations are Proximi.io code speaking those vendors'
     network protocols, not vendor binaries.

     Documentation tooling used to build the SDK (swift-docc-plugin and
     swift-docc-symbolkit, both Apache 2.0) is part of Proximi.io's private
     build only. It is not in the binary and not in the published package
     manifest, so it places no obligation on you.

8.4  If a future release changes this list, the licence file shipped with that
     release states the change. Check the file that came with the version you
     ship.


9. NO WARRANTY

9.1  THE SDK IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY
     KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE IMPLIED
     WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE AND
     NON-INFRINGEMENT.

9.2  Proximi.io does not warrant that the SDK will be uninterrupted or
     error-free, or that any position, heading, floor, geofence event or route
     it produces will be accurate. Indoor positioning is an estimate derived
     from radio and inertial signals, and its accuracy depends on the venue,
     the hardware, the installation and the environment — things outside
     Proximi.io's control.

9.3  You must not use the SDK as the sole means of determining position where
     an error could cause death, personal injury, or serious physical or
     environmental damage. It is not designed, tested or certified for
     navigation of vehicles or aircraft, for medical use, for emergency
     response dispatch, or for any other safety-critical purpose.

9.4  Clause 9 is capitalised because several jurisdictions require a warranty
     disclaimer to be conspicuous for it to take effect. It does not exclude a
     warranty that a mandatory consumer or commercial law gives you and does
     not permit to be excluded.


10. LIABILITY

10.1 Proximi.io is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential
     or punitive damages, nor for lost profits, lost revenue, lost data, or
     business interruption, arising out of or relating to the SDK, however
     caused and on any theory of liability, even if Proximi.io has been advised
     that such damage is possible.

10.2 Proximi.io's total aggregate liability arising out of or relating to the
     SDK and this licence is capped at the amount you paid Proximi.io under
     your commercial agreement in the twelve months before the event giving
     rise to the claim. [CAP — TO BE CONFIRMED: see Open decisions, item 3.]

10.3 Nothing in this licence excludes or limits liability that cannot lawfully
     be excluded or limited, including liability for death or personal injury
     caused by negligence, and for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation.

10.4 You are responsible for your Applications: for what they do with the
     positions the SDK produces, for the permissions they ask of their users,
     and for their compliance with applicable law, Apple's App Store rules, and
     data protection law. You will defend and indemnify Proximi.io against
     third-party claims arising from your Applications, except to the extent
     the claim is caused by the SDK itself.


11. TERM AND TERMINATION

11.1 This licence starts when you first download or use the SDK and runs for as
     long as your commercial agreement with Proximi.io is in force.

11.2 It terminates automatically if your commercial agreement terminates or
     expires. Proximi.io may also terminate it on written notice if you breach
     clause 3 or clause 4 and, where the breach can be cured, do not cure it
     within 30 days of notice.

11.3 On termination you must stop using the SDK in development, stop shipping
     new versions of your Applications that contain it, and delete the copies
     you hold. Proximi.io will not require you to recall or remotely disable
     copies already installed on end users' devices; those copies may remain in
     place, and clauses 3, 5, 8, 9, 10 and 12 keep applying to them.

11.4 Clauses 3, 4.2, 5, 8, 9, 10, 11.3 and 12 survive termination.


12. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTES

12.1 This licence is governed by the laws of [GOVERNING LAW — TO BE DECIDED,
     see Open decisions, item 2], excluding its conflict-of-law rules and
     excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of
     Goods.

12.2 The courts of [FORUM — TO BE DECIDED, see Open decisions, item 2] have
     exclusive jurisdiction, except that either party may seek injunctive
     relief for infringement of intellectual property rights in any competent
     court.

12.3 If your commercial agreement names a governing law or forum, that one
     applies instead, per clause 7.2.


13. GENERAL

13.1 You may not assign this licence without Proximi.io's written consent,
     except to a successor of your whole business, on written notice.

13.2 If a clause is held unenforceable, it is narrowed to the minimum extent
     that makes it enforceable, or struck if it cannot be; the rest stands.

13.3 A delay in enforcing a term is not a waiver of it.

13.4 Proximi.io may publish revised licence terms with a future release. The
     terms shipped in the release you use govern that release; they do not
     change retroactively for releases you already shipped.

13.5 Questions about this licence: support@proximi.io.


